Package: scaleL
Title: Bayesian Imputation of Likert Scale Length for Meta-Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("scaleL", "Authors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "scaleL.pkg@proton.me")
Description: Bayesian imputation of missing Likert scale length L in
    meta-analytic data sets. Combines a variance-bound profile
    likelihood with a structured prior over L (generic, field-specific,
    instrument-specific, or user-supplied) to produce per-study
    posteriors, multiple imputations, and pooled random-effects
    estimates via Rubin's rules. Designed as a lightweight drop-in for
    downstream meta-analysis workflows.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
